DESCRIPTION:For more than 20 years\, The Hummin’ Birds have been bringing the spirit of early American music to life. Born out of Minnesota’s bluegrass and old-time scene\, Cami Harris and Mike Silbernagel honed their sound through late-night jams and festival campfires before winning first place in a 2006 Minnesota State Fair duet contest. Now based in Denver\, the duo shares their signature harmonies\, timeless song interpretations\, and heartfelt originals with audiences across the Front Range and Midwest.\nThis concert is part of the Longmont Museum’s Friday Afternoon Concert Series.  Enjoy an afternoon of live music in our Stewart Auditorium this fall featuring an eclectic array of musical acts from up and down the Front Range.\nLearn more and buy tickets online at https://longmontcolorado.gov/event/the-hummin-birds/ or by calling 303-651-8374.\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/friday-afternoon-concert-the-hummin-birds
DTEND:20260410T223000Z
LOCATION:Longmont Museum
DTSTART:20260410T203000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 [Folk/Acoustic] Friday Afternoon Concert: The Hummin’ Birds
UID:cd71e7a5-598e-4416-a61e-ddb452d14f3c@cd71.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Connected by Music is proud to support Recovery Cafe Longmont with a special concert. This event will feature talented local singer-songwriters:\nMarilyn Walker\nKaren Horan\nRobby Layton\nRecovery Café Longmont is growing and expanding in their capability to support the community. With the purchase and renovation of 801 Main Street\, they will be able to provide more opportunities for community in a healing\, supportive space.\nConnected by Music's organizes rotating benefit shows featuring Front Range musicians supporting their passions. Founder Marilyn Walker is a daughter of an addict\, and her support for Recovery Café Longmont runs deep. "I love what the Recovery Café is bringing to our world - an understanding that a lack of community is the root of the addiction epidemic\, and a trusted model to fix that. We all benefit from living together in a healthy\, mutually-supporting society."\n\nLink: https://www.downtownlongmont.com/do/recovery-cafe-benefit-concert
DTEND:20260425T233000Z
LOCATION:Central Longmont Presbyterian Church
DTSTART:20260425T220000Z
SUMMARY:🎵 Recovery Cafe Benefit Concert
UID:5cf65adf-7f06-42f9-a94f-bb14c85ed04b@5cf6.org
END:VEVENT
